https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ltSiHxxquNo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  A little messy but not too bad once you go over it once or twice.  Lots of Pete Townshend one-strum anchor chords.  Strum each chord in |brackets| just once.  Think of the song in your head as you're playing.  And the strums progress quickly from one verse to the next.

TIP:  The quick |C| - (G) that starts each line is correct but the |C| can be skipped if it's easier.

TIP:  In the bridge you'll play (Dm) and then (D4) so just keep formation and add pinky to 1st string and release to get back to (Dm).  Finally you'll play (D#) which is just (D) up one fret, followed by another (D) so just slide back down.

TIP:  Opening note to sing is the (b) (open 2nd string).
 

